  "id": "COMPOUND:26486 - PROTEIN:6149",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Allamandin may be associated with the High-affinity choline transporter through multiple pathways. LAMA-84, a target of Allamandin, is identified as a target of both (E)-2-(4,5-Dihydroxy-2-{3-[(4-Hydroxyphenethyl)Amino]-3-Oxopropyl}Phenyl)-3-(4-Hydroxy-3,5-Dimethoxyphenyl)-N-(4-Hydroxyphenethyl)Acrylamide and Quercitrin-7-olate, both of which are linked to the High-affinity choline transporter. This indicates that Allamandin may influence the activity of LAMA-84, which in turn affects the choline transporter. The scores from the paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, with some variation in the strength of the evidence across different targets. The mechanism appears to involve the modulation of a target molecule that ultimately interacts with the High-affinity choline transporter, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated.",
